he US where you  get parks like Six Flags and Cedar  Point's putting some really big coasters  next to the parking lots or entrance  areas and this is kind of the same thing  except in real life you obviously never  have a theme park which actually  straddles two sides of a highway and I  say that but it actually does exist  I think ravine flyer too does this for  instance is a coaster that goes across  the highway  there are definitely examples of this  but it's not as common but yeah the  coaster is pretty much finished at this  point I had to keep the layout quite  short because for some reason the  friction of this closed to type is  actually a bit higher than it would be  in real life I think this thing tends to  slow down very quickly I still manage to  get a decent layout out of it I think  but overall its it's not a very long  coaster  and it goes back into the station quite  quickly because I also don't want the  second half of the right to be too slow  so there there's not too much to the  layouts and then everything when it  comes to the scenery around this is all  just very modern and minimalistic I'm  also using some slightly different  foliage and fences and all these kinds  of smaller elements to really help set  this part of the park apart from the  older part which I did realize having a  monorail coaster in the older part  doesn't make much sense because that's a  very relative relatively recent coaster  type but I don't know maybe this exists  in a parallel universe where the  monorail coaster was built earlier than  it is or maybe this is a park in the  future something like that anyway that's  just about it for this park so let's  return to an unpassed mode and to see if  we can make the objectives alright so as  you can see we need to hold the goals  for well three weeks that was originally  to win the scenario so it is another one  of these so we'll be reaching the  objectives very soon but basically this  is the end result of this park and  actually I'm quite happy with this  despite not really having a theme per se  I think there are some pretty charming  areas to this park like the Main Street  / Boulevard area here with these facades  as well as the the area with the vintage  cars and just a new area even though it  looks very different I think very well  fits into the rest of the park as well  and having the skylines of these  coasters line the sides of the highway I  think is really cool too so I'm just  gonna get to the end of the scenario and  then I'll do a last POV of this coaster  here which interestingly to return to  that whole discussion about different  coaster types and Giga coasters and  hyper coasters and mega coasters the  game considers this a Giga coaster which  I guess is a very loose definition which  is just generally based on what coaster  type this is but again this I think this  is not really a Giga coaster because  usually when people talk about Giga  coasters they mean a coaster which is  300 feet in  it's but yeah these these definitions  always kind of depend but just the  overall trend is a coaster that doesn't  invert and that kind of goes out and  back with a lot of airtime and that's  basically what this coaster is doing  anyway we reach the objectives so I  think it's finally a good time to do a  quick POV of this coaster and I know I  keep calling it a POV even though I know  it's sort of off right but for me even  though I don't want to break the  isometric perspective I do think it's  really fun to follow the coasters along  like this so yeah we go from a very  steep drop into a quick tight curve here  which calls a lot of G's very similar to  intimate three or Intimidator 305 into a  small airtime Hill there which is kind  of like the the thing that Hyperion  tends to do a lot and then some airtime  Hills alongside a highway here of course  which according to the game don't pull  that many negative G's but I think you  might definitely get some really good  airtime in this it looks kind of like  ejector airtime but then again I'm not  entirely sure how to tell exactly how  much g-forces you pull on a certain  elements but just from looking these  definitely look like some good airtime  Hills and it started to rain again of  course I haven't mentioned this during  the time lapses but the rain was  actually a major contribution to why I  was struggling to finish this scenario  because while I was trying to make a  profits it kept raining and every time  it rained people wouldn't ride the the  monorail coaster and this is the only  right that made a substantial profits so  because of that it was very difficult to  actually get enough money to build the  hyper coaster without you know letting  the game run for a bit  while I was absent so yeah I don't know  the rain kind of rained on my parade for  this one but I mean I made it in the end  so I'm happy with the end result but  yeah that's basically the park and  actually let's check out the trophy that  we get for this one I remember that you  actually get the bridge plus a part of  the highway but Ananta sure let's  quickly save this end result here and  quits to the main screen but yeah I  think we actually get a highway here  which should be pretty cool alright so  there it is that's  the bridge and then it comes down in  there we don't actually get a highway  next to it but oh we do oh that's super  cool actually came down later and we  even get some cars driving on it whoa  that's cool and the next scenario is  gonna be Oh Orchard acres well that's  one that I've seen quite a few finished  results of that's gonna be a fun one but  I'm not gonna get to that yet I'm sorry  for kind of teasing that one for now I  really really need to get to Biscayne  Beach I think because that's a very  popular scenario and it's one that I've  been looking forward to try for a long  time it's also notoriously difficult so  we'll see how that goes but yeah that's  something to look at in the next episode  for now I want to end this by giving all  of you guys a reminder that I just set  up a discord server at last it was kind  of random that I finally just decided to  make one very impulsive decision but if  you're down to talk about Park attacked  with some other people or with me then  you should totally check out my discord  server out put an invite link in the  description of this video and yeah we  basically talk about planet coaster and  parkzicht and city skylines and  basically all the videos that I make on  my channel so maybe I'll see you guys  there but in any case I hope to see you  guys in the next episode in Biscayne  Beach bye guys
 

